<title>USA: Raytheon gets $52.4 million contract.</title>
<headline>Raytheon gets $52.4 million contract.</headline>
<dateline>BEDFORD, Mass. 1997-02-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Raytheon Co said Tuesday it has won a $52.4 million contract from Motorola Inc for 25 additional shipsets of Iridium main mission antennas.</p>
<p>The Iridium program is a satellite-based worldwide wireless-telephone system.  Raytheon is currenty under contract to develop 80 satellites worth of main mission antennas.</p>
<p>The first delivery of the antennas occurred in December 1995, with the last delivery expected in October 2000. The baseline 66-satellite constellation is expected to be fully deployed by September 1998.</p>
</text>
